-- Sendzz at a glance: the headline figures, both rails, one row per metric.
--
-- Add a single Table visualisation. Nothing to configure.
--
-- Shaped as metric/value rows on purpose. The earlier wide form -- one row, ten columns --
-- needed six separately configured Counters, and every other chart type drew nonsense from it:
-- a pie chart of a single row plots first_activity's epoch milliseconds (1777468671000) as if it
-- were a quantity. Six labelled rows cannot be misread that way.
--
-- Scope: every USDC movement where a Sendzz wallet is one side. On EVM that is enforced by the
-- address filter; on Stellar by the same roster plus our gas station.
--
-- `Bridge movements` counts LEGS, not bridges. A bridge is two events on two chains -- burned
-- where it leaves, minted where it arrives -- so one bridge contributes two. Label it that way;
-- never present bridge_in and bridge_out as separate headline figures. They do not balance
-- (86 bridges begin on Stellar, where the burn is a Soroban call and invisible to a payments
-- query) and an outside reader takes that gap for an error rather than a coverage boundary.
--
-- Fee transfers to our own treasuries are excluded throughout -- this is about user money.
--
-- Verified 2026-09-05: 1,481 transactions, 105,250.82 USDC, 6 chains, from 2026-04-29.

WITH evm AS (
  SELECT tr.blockchain AS chain, tr.block_time AS ts, tr.amount AS usdc,
    CASE
      WHEN tr."from" = 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
        OR tr."from" IN (0xfd78EE919681417d192449715b2594ab58f5D002,
                         0x28b5a0e9C621a5BadaA536219b3a228C8168cf5d,
                         0x81D40F21F12A8F0E3252Bccb954D722d4c464B64) THEN 'bridge_in'
      WHEN tr."to"   = 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
        OR tr."to"   IN (0xfd78EE919681417d192449715b2594ab58f5D002,
                         0x28b5a0e9C621a5BadaA536219b3a228C8168cf5d,
                         0x81D40F21F12A8F0E3252Bccb954D722d4c464B64) THEN 'bridge_out'
      WHEN tr."to"   IN (0x177ce46b514aDe0f552D1C2c54f5De9256CD99b9,
                         0x432bf05E6E63a7e24340AD36148E1a9BCe7A99c2) THEN 'fee'
